rtOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432418">প্ৰয়োগ প্ৰ'গামিং ইণ্টাৰফেচ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11241_1998713_432661"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A character used to control the format of displayed or printed information, rather than to represent a particular letter, digit, or other special character. The space ( ) is one of the more important nonprinting characters.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1998713">non-printable character</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432661">মুদ্ৰণ অযোগ্য বৰ্ণ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11241_85464_432661"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A character used to control the format of displayed or printed information, rather than to represent a particular letter, digit, or other special character. The space ( ) is one of the more important nonprinting characters.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="85464">nonprinting character</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432661">মুদ্ৰণ অযোগ্য বৰ্ণ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun<