ected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1257244">বৈদ্যুতিক চেনচৰ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22043_782590_1257245"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A category of sensor that is used for mechanical measurement of force, scale, pressure, strain, etc.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782590">mechanical sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1257245">যান্ত্ৰিক চেনচৰ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22044_782669_1257246"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A category of sensor that tracks environmental changes such as temperature, atmospheric pressure, humidity, wind speed and wind direction.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782669">environmental sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1257246">পৰিবেশ চেনচৰ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22045_782671_1257247"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of sensor that can determine without physical contact if an object/person is nearby, or can be used to measure the distance between the object/person and the sensor device.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782671">proximity sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1257247">প্ৰক্সিমিটি চেনচৰ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22047_1053912_1257248"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of sensor (such as a proximity sensor) that uses radio frequency identification (RFID) for a numerous purposes, such as identification of physical items, automatic log on, location of people, etc.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1053912">radio frequency identification sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1257248">RFID চেনচৰ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22047_1053912_1257249"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of sensor (such as a proximity sensor) that uses radio frequency identification (RFID) for a numerous purposes, such as identification of physical items, automatic log on, location of people, etc.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1053912">radio frequency identification sensor</term><termNote type="partOfS