ir world of devices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1092267">Live Mesh</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1373046">Live Mesh</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23919_1379736_1373046"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A “software-plus-services” platform and experience that enables PCs and other devices to “come alive” by making them aware of each other through the Internet, enabling individuals and organizations to manage, access, and share their files and applications seamlessly on the Web and across their world of devices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1379736">Windows Live Mesh</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1373046">Live Mesh</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23957_1092760_2847823"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In communications, a channel connecting two switching stations. A trunk usually carries a large number of calls at the same time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1092760">trunk</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2847823">ট্ৰাংক</