7"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The security feature that protects your device by providing startup and runtime protections that the operating system can validate and report on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2615085">System Guard</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2617747">ছিষ্টেম গাৰ্ড</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="46479_2615093_2617751"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The remote attestation service that checks the health of Windows 10-based devices to allow or deny access to networks, apps, or services, based on whether devices prove to be healthy.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2615093">Windows Health Attestation Service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2617751">Windows স্বাস্থ্য সাক্ষ্যদান সেৱা</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="46481_2615123_2617738"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The area in Windows Defender Security Center that helps customers keep their devices refreshed and up to date with the latest version of Windows 10. Device health advisor monitors the device and provides information and recommendations in a Health report to address common issues 