amically configure the data-link layer of a PPP connection.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="175156">LCP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="433149">লিংক নিয়ন্ত্ৰণ প্ৰ'ট'ক'ল</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6835_175156_433150"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A PPP control protocol that negotiates link and PPP parameters to dynamically configure the data-link layer of a PPP connection.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="175156">LCP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="433150">LCP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6841_139625_1852626"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A shape in an organization chart that is next to another shape that is connected to the same superior (or manager) shape.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="139625">coworker shape</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1852626">সহকৰ্মী আকৃতি</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6842_2656621_2657650"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A lightweight version of Outlook Web Access optimized for accessibility and compatibility with the widest array of browsers and operating systems.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2656621">Outlook Web App Light</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2657650">Outlook Web App Light</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6846_14902_3145841"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The arrangement of a sequence of items from lowest to highest, such as from 1 to 10 or from A to Z. The rules for determining ascending order in a particular application can be very complicated: capital letters before lowercase letters, extended ASCII characters in ASCII order, and so on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="14902">ascending order</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3145841">A-ৰ পৰা Z-লৈ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6846_3144701_3145841"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The arrangement of a sequence of items from lowest to highest, such as from 1 to 10 or from A to Z. The rules for determining ascending order in a particular application can be very complicated: capital letters before lowercase letters, extended ASCII characters in ASCII order, and so on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3144701">A to Z</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3145841">A-ৰ পৰা Z-লৈ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6856_318782_433809"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The ! character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318782">exclamation point</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="433809">ভাৱবোধক বিন্দু</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6866_232823_1852764"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An HTML format with Microsoft Office-specific tags removed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232823">filtered HTML</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1852764">ফিল্টাৰ কৰা HTML</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6867_121727_432866"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A certification specifying that a particular message existed at a specific time and date. In a digital context, trusted third parties generate a trusted time stamp for a particular message by having a time stamping service append a time value to a message and then digitally signing the result.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="121727">time stamp</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432866">সময় মোহৰ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6879_78424_432617"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Moving text that is used on a data access page to draw the user's attention to a specific page element, such as a headline or an important announcement.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="78424">marquee</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432617">মাৰ্কীউ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6883_210434_433215"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A device used to copy files to recordable CDs and DVDs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="210434">disc burner</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="433215">ডিস্ক বাৰ্নাৰ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6886_2911_432047"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A communications device that converts between digital data from a computer or terminal and analog audio signals that can pass through a standard telephone line.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2911">modem</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432047">মডেম</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6886_2911_432048"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A communications device that converts between digital data from a computer or terminal and analog audio signals that can pass through a standard telephone line.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2911">modem</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432048">মডুলেটৰ/ডিমডুলেটৰ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6886_2912_432047"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A communications device that converts between digital data from a computer or terminal and analog audio signals that can pass through a standard telephone line.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2912">modulator/demodulator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432047">মডেম</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6886_2912_432048"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A communications device that converts between digital data from a computer or terminal and analog audio signals that can pass through a standard telephone line.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2912">modulator/demodulator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432048">মডুলেটৰ/ডিমডুলেটৰ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="689_108242_432781"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">On the IBM PC/XT and AT and compatible keyboards, a key on the top row of the numeric keypad that controls the effect of the cursor control keys and sometimes prevents the screen from scrolling. On the enhanced and Macintosh keyboards, this key is to the right of the function keys on the top row. Many modern applications ignore the Scroll Lock setting.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="108242">SCROLL LOCK key</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432781">SCROLL LOCK কী</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6894_318712_433788"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A statement that the text or program code contained within the item on which the notice appears is the intellectual property of Microsoft (or other entity).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318712">copyright notice</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="433788">কপিৰাইট জাননী</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6904_108595_1519028"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To try to locate something (a file, a folder, a computer, a text).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="108595">search</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1519028">অনুসন্ধান কৰক</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6904_644853_1519028"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip typ