 is not a whole number, such as ½ (vulgar fraction) or 0.5 (decimal fraction), formed by dividing one quantity into another.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="56463">fraction</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1256982">ভগ্নাংশ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8916_1034316_1519062"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file containing digitized audio, such as voice or music.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1034316">audio</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1519062">অডিঅ’</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8916_1034316_2289688"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file containing digitized audio, such as voice or music.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1034316">audio</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2289688">অডিঅ'</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8916_16592_1519062"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file containing digitized audio, such as voice or music.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="16592">audio file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1519062">অডিঅ’</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8916_16592_2289688"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file containing digitized audio, such as voice or music.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="16592">audio file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2289688">অডিঅ'</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="892_2455_432037"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A binary number that uniquely identifies a host (computer) connected to the Internet to other Internet hosts, for the purposes of communication through the transfer of packets.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2455">IP address</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432037">IP ঠিকনা</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="892_725809_432037"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A binary number that uniquely identifies a host (computer) connected to the Internet to other Internet hosts, for the purposes of communication through the transfer of packets.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="725809">Internet Protocol address</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432037">IP ঠিকনা</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8922_34048_432274"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A startup process that begins with turning on the computer's power. Typically, a cold boot involves some basic hardware checking by the system, after which the operating system is loaded from disk into memory.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="34048">cold boot</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432274">ক'ল্ড বুট</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8922_34048_432275"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A startup process that begins with turning on the computer's power. Typically, a cold boot involves some basic hardware checking by the system, after which the operating system is loaded from disk into memory.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="34048">cold boot</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432275">ক'ল্ড আৰম্ভ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8922_34049_432274"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A startup process that begins with turning on the computer's power. Typically, a cold boot involves some basic hardware checking by the system, after which the operating system is loaded from disk into memory.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="34049">cold start</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432274">ক'ল্ড বুট</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8922_34049_432275"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A startup process that begins with turning on the computer's power. Typically, a cold boot involves some basic hardware checking by the system, after which the operating system is loaded from disk into memory.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="34049">cold start</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432275">ক'ল্ড আৰম্ভ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8924_112244_432799"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The command interpreter that is used to pass commands to the operating system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="112244">shell</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432799">শ্বেল</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8929_81571_432635"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A device on which images generated by the computer's video adapter are displayed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="81571">monitor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432635">মনিটৰ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8931_84940_1989220"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of one or more COM objects in a process. A COM object lives in exactly one apartment, in the sense that its methods can legally be directly called only by a thread that belongs to that apartment. Any other thread that wants to call the object must go through a proxy.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="84940">apartment</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1989220">এপাৰ্টমেণ্ট</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8945_117177_432836"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An index entry that falls under a more general heading. For example, the index entry "planets" could have the subentries "Mars" and "Venus."</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="117177">subentry</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432836">উপ-প্রবিষ্ট</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8949_140209_432991"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Related data points that are plotted in a chart. Each data series in a chart has a unique color or pattern and is represented in the chart legend. You can plot one or more data series in a chart. Pie charts have only one data series.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="140209">data series</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432991">ডাটা ক্রম</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8949_1508235_432991"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Related data points that are plotted in a chart. Each data series in a chart has a unique color or pattern and is represented in the chart legend. You can plot one or more data series in a chart. Pie charts have only one data series.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1508235">series</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432991">ডাটা ক্রম</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8960_545680_1852820"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A view of a document as it will appear on the printed page.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="545680">page layout view</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1852820">পৃষ্ঠা লেআউট দৰ্শন</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8960_545691_1852820"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A view of a document as it will appear on the printed page.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="545691">print layout view</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1852820">পৃষ্ঠা লেআউট দৰ্শন</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8961_318125_433752"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Colors that are directly next to each other on the color wheel. Each color has two analogous colors (one on each side of it).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318125">analogous colors</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="433752">অনুৰূপ ৰং</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8983_61675_1852565"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A fixed-disk file system that organizes the disk into volumes, rather than partitions and logical drives. HPFS supports long, mixed-case filenames and extended attributes, and implements several levels of caching, for improved operating-system performance. The IBM OS/2 operating system supports HPFS.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="61675">high performance file system</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1852565">HPFS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8983_61676_1852565"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A fixed-disk file system that organizes the disk into volumes, rather than partitions and logical drives. HPFS supports long, mixed-case filenames and extended attributes, and implements several levels of caching, for improved operating-system performance. The IBM OS/2 operating system supports HPFS.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="61676">high-performance file system</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1852565">HPFS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8983_61677_1852565"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A fixed-disk file system that organizes the disk into volumes, rather than partitions and logical drives. HPFS supports long, mixed-case filenames and extended attributes, and implements several levels of caching, for improved operating-system performance. The IBM OS/2 operating system supports HPFS.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="61677">HPFS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1852565">HPFS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9010_347945_433968"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group in the data source that can occur more than once. Controls such as repeating sections and repeating tables are bound to repeating groups.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="347945">repeating group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="433968">পুনঃ উদ্ভুত গোট</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9025_253693_1804336"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A data type that stores a signed, exact numeric value described as the number of digits appearing before and after the decimal point, with a maximum of 29 total digits. All possible digits cannot be represented if you are using the maximum number of digits.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="253693">Decimal</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1804336">দশমিক</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9026_44196_1258472"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of rewriting parts of a file to contiguous sectors on a hard disk to increase the speed of access and retrieval.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="44196">defragmentation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1258472">খণ্ড-বিখণ্ডকৰণ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9028_143088_433018"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The blank area between two or more columns of text or between two facing pages in a publication.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="143088">gutter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="433018">লোৰ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9030_146463_1852675"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a 2-D chart, the area bounded by the axes, including all data series. In a 3-D chart, the area bounded by the axes, including the data series, category names, tick-mark labels, and axis titles.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="146463">plot area</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1852675">প্ল'ট ক্ষেত্ৰ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9035_13104_432128"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A small piece of code that can be transported over the Internet and executed on the recipient's machine. The term is especially used to refer to such programs as they are embedded in line as objects in HTML documents on the World Wide Web.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="13104">applet</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432128">এপলেট</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9064_232419_1852754"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The alternate calendar that is selected from within Outlook. The secondary calendar appears when dual calendar support is enabled.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232419">secondary calendar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1852754">দ্বিতীয় কেলেণ্ডাৰ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9067_3665_432060"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software package that replaces an existing version of a product or a feature with a newer and/or more powerful or sophisticated version of the same product or feature. The upgrade process typically leaves existing customer data and preferences intact while replacing the existing software with the newer version.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3665">upgrade</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432060">নবীকৰণ</t