Note><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9067_3666_432061"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software package that replaces an existing version of a product or a feature with a newer and/or more powerful or sophisticated version of the same product or feature. The upgrade process typically leaves existing customer data and preferences intact while replacing the existing software with the newer version.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3666">software upgrade</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="432061">ছফটৱেৰ নবীকৰণ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9073_144243_433026"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The condition of a field, record, recordset, or database that makes it read-only to all users except the user currently modifying it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="144243">locked</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="as-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="433026">অৱৰোধিত</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9074_118405_432840"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The rules governing the formation of a command-line statement, including the order in which a command must